<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="157" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>External SPA grids stop offering the internal MDA views (showViewSelector=false), and each external module's column allow-list shrinks to what its grid actually shows (owner round 4 item 7, task 134 open item D1)</title>
    <phase>Session 27 — UAC defect remediation (owner round 4, 2026-10-01)</phase>
    <gate>startable now (134 merged)</gate>
    <status>completed-with-escalation</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Narrows the columns an external (CIAM/contact) caller may read through /fetch and /record. That is an authorization surface (defect C6), plus a client change to the external SPA.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The change touches an authorization allow-list on the external data plane. If a list is shrunk wrongly, it either leaks or blanks a grid.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>It edits ExternalAccessModule.cs descriptor allow-lists (task 134's surface) and the external SPA grid mounts.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>134</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, security, external-spa, react</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Task 134 open item D1 (notes/task-134-*.md). Owner round 4 item 7 (2026-10-01): "yes".</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Turn off the view picker on every external SPA grid, then shrink each external module's server column allow-list. The new list is the columns that grid's own configuration shows, plus the scope columns and the /record default projection, and nothing more.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: the external data plane (ExternalModuleDataEndpoints and ExternalAccessModule descriptors) and the external SPA (React, DataGrid framework).</role>

  <goal>Every `&lt;DataGrid&gt;` mounted in `src/client/external-spa` passes `showViewSelector={false}`. External callers can therefore no longer switch a grid to an internal MDA saved view. Each external module descriptor's column allow-list then drops the columns admitted only by derivation rule (b) of task 134, the sibling saved views the ViewSelector offered. It keeps (a) every attribute the module's `sprk_gridconfiguration` references, (c) the scope-dimension attributes, and (d) the /record default projection. The derivation is re-done from LIVE data (read-only) and recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 134 (defect C6) gave every external module a column allow-list. At the time the external grids still offered a ViewSelector over the entity's internal MDA main views, so rule (b) had to admit the columns of every sibling view that could render rows. That widened each list beyond what the grid's own configuration shows. The owner approved removing the selector (round 4 item 7), so rule (b) no longer applies and the lists can shrink.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/widgets/GridWidgetBody.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/pages/OutsideCounselDashboard.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/ContactsOrganizations.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/DocumentLibrary.tsx</file>
      <file role="read">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/DataGrid.tsx</file>
      <file role="read">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ExternalModuleColumnAllowListTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Derive each new list from LIVE data, read-only (the module's sprk_gridconfiguration record, the scope dimensions and EntityDefinitions for the primary id and primary name). Never write a list from memory. Record the derivation per module in the task note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Shrink ONLY. A column absent from the old list must not appear in the new one. A column the grid configuration references must not be dropped, or the grid blanks.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every external DataGrid mount in src/client/external-spa gets showViewSelector={false}. The shared DataGrid's default (true) does not change, because internal surfaces still use the selector.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Deployment order is recorded in the note: the external SPA (no selector) deploys BEFORE or WITH the BFF that shrinks the lists. A BFF-first deploy would make a still-offered view error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The external SPA build is npm run build:prod (or the package's documented prod build). Use npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund, never npm ci.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">ADR-038 test bans. Prove the shrink bites by seeding a dropped column back.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Grep every DataGrid mount under src/client/external-spa and set showViewSelector={false}; build the SPA.</step>
    <step order="2">For each external module descriptor, re-derive (a)+(c)+(d) live, read-only; compute the drop set (old list minus new); record both in notes/task-157-external-grid-columns.md.</step>
    <step order="3">Apply the shrunk lists; update ExternalModuleColumnAllowListTests so each module's list equals its recorded derivation, and add a test that a column admitted only by rule (b) is now refused by /fetch and stripped by /record.</step>
    <step order="4">Run affected tests, the full BFF unit suite and NetArchTest; record the deployment order.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every DataGrid mount under src/client/external-spa passes showViewSelector={false} (asserted by a source scan test or the SPA's own tests); the shared DataGrid default is unchanged; the SPA prod build succeeds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each external module's allow-list equals its recorded live derivation (a)+(c)+(d); no column was added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a column that was admitted only by rule (b) is refused by /fetch and stripped from /record for that module.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every column the module's grid configuration references is still admitted (no grid blanks).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The shrink is proven to bite by seeding a dropped column back; BFF unit + NetArchTest green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, after deploying SPA then BFF): an outside-counsel contact opens each external grid; no view selector shows; each grid renders its configured columns.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A grid's live configuration references a column that is an SPE pointer or FLS-secured (task 134's refused classes) — STOP and report; do not admit it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes>Owner round 4 item 7 (2026-10-01). Closes task 134's open item D1.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>FULL rigor; code-review and adr-check at Step 9.5.</protocol>
    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-157">
      Code complete. The live deploy and the MANUAL live gate are PENDING; no live write was made.
      Client: the one Spaarke DataGrid mount (GridWidgetBody.tsx) passes showViewSelector={false}. The shared default
      is unchanged. Premise correction: OutsideCounselDashboard, ContactsOrganizations and DocumentLibrary mount
      Fluent's DataGrid, which has no view picker, so they are untouched. The SPA has no build:prod; npm run build
      (vite build) succeeds.
      Server: lists re-derived READ-ONLY from live dev on 2026-10-01 from the six grid configjson records,
      EntityDefinitions and IsSecured. The escalation trigger did not fire: there are no pointer columns and no
      FLS-secured columns. 16 rule-(b)-only columns were dropped across project, invoice, work assignment and
      matter. Documents, service requests and grid configuration are unchanged. No column was added.
      Tests: ExternalModuleColumnAllowListTests section 6 has an equality pin per module, a shrink-only check
      against the task-134 lists, and fetch-400 / record-$select-400 / record-strip for each dropped column. A new
      arch guard, ExternalSpaGridViewSelectorGuardTests, has controls.
      Perturbations P1-P3 each turned tests red (1 / 4 / 7) and were reverted.
      No new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, job or package; the change is data in the existing
      registrations, so the section 11 justification is n/a.
      Deploy order: SPA first, or together with the BFF. Full record:
      notes/task-157-external-grid-columns.md.
    </outcome>
    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-157-r1" round="review-1">
      Status corrected from "completed" to "completed-with-escalation". Code is complete and tested. Two items stay
      open: the MANUAL live gate (criterion 6, pending by design, deploy order in note section 5), and an owner
      decision on finding F1.
      Item 8/15 (guard failed open, criterion 1): ExternalSpaGridViewSelectorGuardTests was rewritten to fail closed.
      Every import of DataGrid or DataGridDefault from the shared lib is now a mount source. That covers named,
      aliased, "default as", default and mixed default+named imports, from the package alias or from a path into
      Spaarke.UI.Components. Each mount must end with showViewSelector={false} as its last top-level attribute, with
      no spread after it. Any non-JSX reference to the grid binding is refused (createElement, aliasing,
      export { X }, export default X, HOCs). Also refused: DataGridPageShell(Default), namespace imports,
      re-exports that could carry the grid, dynamic import()/require() of the shared lib, and unparseable import
      clauses. Each of the verifier's shapes A-H, plus D2/D3/E2/F2-F4/G2/H2, a relative path and an unparseable
      clause, has a Theory control row. A positive control covers spread-before, closing tag, typeof, type-only
      re-export and the JSX comment. The verifier's nine seed files were re-created under
      external-spa/src/zzseed. The production fact went red with 8 violations, one per shape (F was caught via
      F_reexport.ts). The seeds were then deleted. P1 was re-run against the new detector: red at
      GridWidgetBody.tsx:71, then restored (no diff) and touched.
      Item 10 (comment stripper failed open): only comments that START their line are stripped now, so a "/*" or
      "//" inside a string can no longer blank code. The new control covers 'src/**/*.ts' and 'a // b'.
      Item 9 (no run counts): counts are recorded below and in note section 7.
      Runs (this branch): ExternalSpaGridViewSelectorGuardTests 29/29. NetArchTest (dotnet test
      tests/Spaarke.ArchTests): Passed 370, Failed 0, Total 370. That is 349 at 3d858490b plus 21 new control rows.
      BFF unit (dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests): Passed 13627, Failed 0, Skipped 54, Total 13681 (Debug, 20m24s). The verifier's own run at 3d858490b
      (Release) was Passed 13627, Failed 0, Skipped 54, Total 13681.
      SPA: no client file changed in this round (GridWidgetBody.tsx is byte-identical to 3d858490b). The
      verifier's npm run build (vite) at 3d858490b exited 0, so no rebuild was needed.
      Item 11 (INFO): the task-134 comparison test is tautological on its own. It reaches production only through
      the equality pin, which the verifier confirmed against live data. Left as is.
      Item 12 / F1 (OPEN, owner decision): with the selector off, DataGrid still calls the external savedqueries
      route on every load, so internal MDA view definitions still reach external callers. Proposed follow-up:
      skip the sibling fetch when showViewSelector is false, and/or restrict the external savedquer* routes. This
      is out of scope here.
      Item 16 (OPEN, live gate): deploy the SPA first (gh workflow run deploy-external-spa.yml --ref
      &lt;branch&gt;), then the BFF (pwsh scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1), then run note section 6. Not run here: no
      live write was made.
      Justification: no new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, job or package. Only a test file and
      documentation changed.
    </outcome>
    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-157-r1-r2" round="review-2">
      Status stays "completed-with-escalation". The same two items stay open: the MANUAL live gate (criterion 6,
      pending by design) and the owner decision on F1.
      Item 5/9 (guard still failed open, criterion 1): ExternalSpaGridViewSelectorGuardTests now refuses all five
      seeded shapes.
      S1, a generic mount (&lt;DataGrid&lt;any&gt;): a mount is now "&lt;X" followed by anything that cannot
      continue the identifier. Type arguments are refused.
      S2/S3, a JSX-children line starting "//" or "/*": comments are no longer stripped; every comment is scanned
      as code. GridWidgetBody.tsx's JSDoc was reworded so no comment names the binding (comments only; the mount
      line is unchanged).
      S4, a brace inside a string attribute: the opening-tag walk now skips string literals as strings. It refuses
      an attribute string holding { } &lt; &gt;, a JS string or template literal holding { } inside a prop
      expression, any "/" except the closing "/&gt;", a bare JSX element as an attribute value, an unbalanced }, and
      a tag that never closes. A bare showViewSelector after the false one counts as true. A namespaced
      x:showViewSelector does not count.
      S5, a node_modules-relative import: the shared-library pattern now matches @spaarke/ui-components or
      Spaarke.UI.Components anywhere in the specifier.
      Each shape has a Theory control row: 16 rows covering S1-S5 plus the neighbours above. The comment control now
      asserts that comments ARE reported. The sanctioned control drops its JSX comment and adds a second compliant
      mount: a plain string attribute, a nested arrow prop, "{ false }" and "/ &gt;".
      Seeded under external-spa/src/zzseed (S1-S5 verbatim plus 5 extras), the production fact went red with 10
      violations, one per mount. The seeds were then deleted. P1 re-run: red at GridWidgetBody.tsx:73, then
      restored and touched.
      Item 7 (INFO): F1 is still open for the owner. The task-134 comparison test is tautological on its own, as
      acknowledged. No change.
      Item 10 (live gate): unchanged. Deploy the SPA first (gh workflow run deploy-external-spa.yml --ref
      &lt;branch&gt;), then the BFF (pwsh scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1), then run note section 6. Not run here: no
      live write was made.
      Runs: guard 45/45; NetArchTest Passed 386, Failed 0, Total 386; BFF unit Passed 13627, Failed 0, Skipped 54, Total 13681 (Debug, 22m15s); SPA npm run build
      (vite) exit 0.
      Justification: no new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, job or package. Changes: one test file,
      comment-only edits to one client file, and documentation.
    </outcome>
    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-157-b1" round="review-3">
      Status stays "completed-with-escalation". Two items stay open: the MANUAL live gate (criterion 6, pending by
      design) and the owner decision on F1.
      BLOCKING item (criterion 1, the guard failed open a third time). The verifier compiled three shapes with
      vite build into a live mount with the picker on: V1 import.meta.glob of DataGrid.tsx, V2 a unicode-escaped
      identifier, and V3 React.cloneElement over a compliant mount. A regex cannot catch V3 in general (a computed
      property such as React['clone' + 'Element'] spells nothing), so the guarantee now rests on a runtime guard.
      Runtime guard: the new src/client/external-spa/src/widgets/ExternalDataGrid.tsx renders the shared grid as
      DataGrid {...props} showViewSelector={false}, with the forced false AFTER the caller's props. Its props type
      omits showViewSelector. A clone or createElement of ExternalDataGrid sets the wrapper's props, and the forced
      false still wins. GridWidgetBody.tsx now mounts ExternalDataGrid; its header comment was updated. The bundle
      (dist/assets/app.js) shows e=&gt;u.jsx(ole,{...e,showViewSelector:!1}), and showViewSelector:!0 occurs
      nowhere in it.
      Scan: ExternalSpaGridViewSelectorGuardTests now enforces six rules.
      1. Only ExternalDataGrid.tsx may import a grid binding. A fully compliant mount in any other file is
         refused.
      2. The wrapper's text is pinned, whitespace-insensitive. A computed clone inside the wrapper passes every
         regex rule but fails the pin (P5).
      3. import.meta.glob is refused in any form (V1, plus the spaced, bracket and globEager forms).
      4. In a grid-binding file, cloneElement, createElement and any \u escape are refused (V2, V3).
      5. Every from '...' specifier must be escape-free. One that names the shared library must belong to a parsed
         import, which catches the string-named specifier { "DataGrid" as G }. It must resolve inside the SPA
         source or into the library. A bare @spaarke/ specifier must be the library.
      6. Every import() or require() takes one plain literal that resolves inside the SPA source.
      New fact SharedLibrary_OnlyKnownModulesCarryTheGrid pins the four shared-library modules that import or
      re-export the grid: DataGrid/index.ts, DataGridPageShell.tsx, components/index.ts and src/index.ts.
      Without that pin, a new shared component that embeds the grid would reach the SPA unseen; the scan
      refuses DataGridPageShell only by name.
      Controls: 23 round-3 Theory rows (V1-V1e, V2-V2e, V3-V3c, W1-W5, X1-X4, Y1). There is also a sanctioned
      external-SPA control (it uses the wrapper, local dynamic imports, @/ and npm imports, and Array.from) and a
      fan-in control. The round-1 and round-2 rows now run AS the wrapper, so each still proves its own rule fires.
      Proof the guard bites:
      - Nine seed files under external-spa/src/zzseed (V1, V2, V3, a clone of ExternalDataGrid, a string-named
        specifier, an escaped module specifier, a module outside the SPA, a dynamic variable import, and a
        compliant mount outside the wrapper). The production fact went red with 10 violations across the 8
        bypass files. The clone of ExternalDataGrid was correctly NOT flagged, because the runtime guard
        neutralises it. The seeds were deleted.
      - P4 (spread moved after the forced prop in the wrapper): the production fact and the pin both went red.
      - P5 (a computed clone inside the wrapper): only the pin went red. That is the scan's residual, closed by
        the pin.
      - P1 (GridWidgetBody imports the shared grid directly, compliant JSX): the production fact went red.
      - P6 (a new shared component imports the grid as Table): the fan-in fact went red.
      Each perturbation was restored from a hash-checked backup and touched.
      MINOR item (overclaims): the ExternalAccessModule.cs derivation comment (comment only) no longer says the
      guard "fails the build otherwise". It now names the runtime wrapper and the guard's documented residuals,
      and says the allow-list refuses regardless. The guard's remarks no longer claim the scan refuses
      everything; they say three rounds each found a bypass and list the residuals. Note section 7 records round
      3 without a "no remaining shape" claim.
      Residuals (documented in the guard remarks and in note G5):
      - a new npm dependency that bundles and re-exports the grid;
      - a shared-library import() whose path is built in a variable elsewhere;
      - edits to the shared DataGrid.tsx itself.
      All three are reviewed changes outside external-spa/src, and the BFF allow-list still returns 400 for the
      internal views' columns.
      CONFIRMED / INFO / CLEAN items: no change needed. F1 stays OPEN for the owner.
      Section 11 justification for the new file ExternalDataGrid.tsx:
      (1) Existing: GridWidgetBody.tsx mounted the shared grid directly. DataGridPageShell also wraps the grid but
      forces the picker ON, and Grep shows no other wrapper.
      (2) Extension: the shared DataGrid's default cannot change, because internal surfaces keep the picker (a
      task constraint). Forcing the prop inside GridWidgetBody would leave an 80-line file as the only grid
      importer, and its text is too large to pin. A 20-line pinned wrapper is the smallest unit the guard can
      hold exactly.
      (3) Cost of doing nothing: the three verifier shapes compile into a live mount with the picker on, and the
      guard passes them.
      Section 10: no BFF surface was added. The BFF edit is comment-only (no IL change), so the publish size was
      not re-measured.
      Runs: see note section 7 (round 3).
    </outcome>
  </execution>
</task>
